## Course overview

Mathematics: Applications and Interpretation (AI) suits students who enjoy seeing mathematics used to describe and solve real-world problems. It emphasises modelling, statistics, and the confident use of technology - good preparation for the social sciences, natural sciences, design, business, and economics.

## What you will study

- **Number and algebra**.
- **Functions**: modelling real situations.
- **Geometry and trigonometry**.
- **Statistics and probability**: a major focus, extended at HL.
- **Calculus**: applied differentiation and integration.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | HL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (calculator) | 40% | 30% | Short questions |
| Paper 2 (calculator) | 40% | 30% | Extended questions |
| Paper 3 (HL) | - | 20% | Extended modelling problems |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | 20% | A mathematical exploration on a topic of choice |

> Choose **AI** if you prefer applied, data-driven mathematics; choose **AA** if you prefer proof and pure mathematics.
